Project: PolicyCompare — Backend Prompt

Goal
- Generate a Python backend (FastAPI) that provides policy data and comparison APIs. Include an easy-to-run local data store (SQLite) and instructions to switch to Postgres for production.
- Provide seed data and a simple admin script to import policies from JSON/CSV.

Is a DB required?
- For any non-trivial app that stores policies persistently, a DB is recommended. For a prototype or single-developer local app, SQLite is perfectly sufficient (lightweight, zero-config, ACID).
- Recommendation: Use SQLite for local/dev (default). For production or multi-user concurrency, use Postgres.

Stack & Tooling
- Python 3.10+
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn for server
- SQLModel (or SQLAlchemy + pydantic) for ORM + models (recommend SQLModel for DX)
- Alembic optional for migrations (note: SQLModel + Alembic config)
- Requirements: `fastapi uvicorn[standard] sqlmodel databases[sqlite] pydantic` (provide `requirements.txt`)

API Spec
- GET /api/policies
  - Query params: page, page_size, q (search), tags (comma list)
  - Returns paginated list of policies
- GET /api/policies/{id}
  - Returns detailed policy
- POST /api/compare
  - Body: { ids: string[] } (limit 2-4)
  - Returns combined object for UI consumption (aligned sections, diff hints)
- POST /api/seed (dev-only)
  - Seeds DB from provided JSON file

Data Model (SQLModel)
- Policy: id (uuid), title, description, effective_date (date), issuer, tags (JSON/text), sections (JSON), last_updated, source_url
- Section: represented as a nested JSON list inside Policy for simplicity (avoid separate table initially)

Implementation Details
- Enable CORS for local frontend (`VITE_API_URL` origin)
- Provide dependency for DB session and clean teardown
- Validation: enforce compare IDs limit to 4 and return 400 if exceeded
- Provide a `scripts/seed.py` to populate sample policies (10-20 items) with realistic fields
- Provide OpenAPI docs (FastAPI auto-docs)

Dev & Run Commands (generate)
- `python -m venv .venv`
- `pip install -r requirements.txt`
- `uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000`

Deliverables when this prompt is executed
- A runnable FastAPI project with SQLModel + SQLite integration, seed script, tests for endpoints, and clear README with run instructions and how to switch to Postgres.

Notes for automated generator
- Keep file structure clear: `app/main.py`, `app/models.py`, `app/crud.py`, `app/schemas.py`, `app/api.py`, `scripts/seed.py`, `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile` (optional).
- Add meaningful error handling and input validation.
- Ensure CORS and environment-driven config for DB URL.

End of backend prompt.